        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "RFC: Claws",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Defines Claws as starter setup manifests for runnable OpenClaw agent setups.\n- Keeps Claws distinct from plugin-bundled skills and RFC 0009 feeds while reusing feeds for discovery/curation.\n- Documents the authored OpenClaw stack through export, skills, MCP, and doctor diagnostics; connector installers are no longer part of the first-series plan and remain preview-only/fail-closed until OpenClaw has a connector-owned setup surface.\n- Keeps ClawHub and automation as separate follow-up tracks.\n\n## Current OpenClaw Stack\n\n1. openclaw/openclaw#101328: validation lifecycle\n2. openclaw/openclaw#101755: consent-gated apply and artifact provenance\n3. openclaw/openclaw#101973: workspace/persona apply\n4. openclaw/openclaw#102228: plugin artifact installers and uninstall warnings\n5. openclaw/openclaw#102296: status/remove lifecycle\n6. openclaw/openclaw#102306: export authoring\n7. openclaw/openclaw#102383: skill artifacts\n8. openclaw/openclaw#102406: MCP artifacts\n9. openclaw/openclaw#102427: doctor diagnostics\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- Manual RFC consistency scan for stale connector-installer plan language\r\n",
